{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py:373-390 _activation_map` accepts `\"activate\": [\"project.x\"]` (legacy) alongside the canonical `{\"project.x\": [\"plan_review\"]}`; the repo's own overlay uses the canonical form, but client projects' `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` files may use the list form. Operator ruling: keep accepting it, warn. No `logging` or `warnings` idiom exists in `criteria/` (grep: zero). The repo's single deprecation channel is `_deprecations.warn_deprecated` (`src/rebar/_deprecations.py:17-21,386-413`; `tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py:134` fails any raw `.warning(\"… is deprecated\")`), emitting `logger.warning` on the caller's module logger. `effective_criteria` has 17 src call sites, so the emission rides the existing `(gate_key, repo_root, overlay-signature)` `lru_cache` at `overlay.py:333` to fire once per overlay content. Separately, two comments still described the single-pass review engine that `a256-1ae4-cf3d-4711` deleted: `src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py:135` named it as a second producer of `REVIEW_RESULT`, and `src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py:9-15` tied this module's self-containment to a `code_review.single_pass` route and a lazy re-export that no longer exist. Cites for steps 1-4 are on origin/main 38f8587f65d.\n\n## Follow-up scope: the missing release-notes entry\nSteps 1-4 landed as `48c913d93d9` (Gerrit change 3166, `LLM-Review +1` + `Verified +1`, 9 paths); ACs 1-6 were re-measured on that landed tree and hold. This story is reopened for one omission it owns.\n\nParent epic `87d8-8bb6-5226-4a5b` AC5 requires that **every client-facing change carries a release-notes line**, and `docs/release-notes.md` is where this epic's siblings put theirs. Attributing each of the epic's 18 children by its `rebar-ticket:` trailer, **10** landed a commit touching that file. Of the 8 that did not, 7 have no client-visible surface — `34ec`/`d0af`/`8c31` repoint tests or docs, `f7bd`/`dbac` fix a comment and a self-description, `dc42` deletes private scaffolding, and `a256`'s own deliverables are already covered by the `rebar.llm.operations` and `rebar.llm.aggregate` entries its sibling changes added. The 8th is this story. Step 2 is client-facing in exactly the sense the file's own header describes (\"agent-visible *contract* changes\"): a project whose `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` still uses the bare id-list form begins emitting a `logger.warning` it never emitted before, on logger `rebar.llm.criteria.overlay`, scheduled for removal in v1.0.0. `48c913d93d9` touched no release-notes file, and on `origin/main` both `git grep -c activate` and `git grep -c criteria_routing` over `docs/release-notes.md` return **0** hits. So epic AC5 is not met while this gap stands, and this story is the one that left it.\n\nThe file is newest-first: `# Release notes` at `:1`, the header note at `:3-5`, the intro paragraph at `:7-9`, a blank at `:10`, and the current newest entry `## Warn-class tombstones are retired, and unknown ``[llm]`` keys are reported` at `:11`. It holds **64** `##` sections. New entries are inserted after `:10`, ahead of the previous newest — the pattern `5cd7e2784ab` used (`@@ -8,6 +8,28 @@`).\n\n## Approach\nSteps 1-4 are **landed** in `48c913d93d9` and are restated here only as the record of what this ticket delivered; they are not re-executed.\n\n1. `_deprecations.py` `_ENTRIES`: added `_scheduled(\"cfg\", \"criteria_routing.json 'activate' id-list\", …)`, rendering as \"criteria_routing.json 'activate' id-list is deprecated; use the {...} mapping form (scheduled for removal in v1.0.0).\"\n2. `overlay.py`: added `import logging` + a module `logger`, and in `_effective_routing_cached` right after `overlay = _load_overlay(rr_arg)` / `if overlay is not None:` a `warn_deprecated(...)` guarded by `isinstance(overlay.get(\"activate\"), list)`. `_activation_map` unchanged.\n3. Corrected the two stale single-pass comments in `schemas/__init__.py` and `code_review/assemble.py` (comment text only).\n4. `docs/plan-review-gate.md` gained one sentence: \"A bare id list … is still accepted and infers the gate from the routing maps, but logs a deprecation warning.\"\n\n5. **Remaining.** Insert one new `##` section into `docs/release-notes.md` immediately after the intro blank at `:10`, so it becomes the newest entry and the existing `## Warn-class tombstones …` section follows it unchanged. The section records, for an agent or a different rebar version reading this store: that the bare id-list spelling of `activate` in `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` is now deprecated and warns; that it is still honoured and resolves exactly as before, so no routing behaviour changes; that the warning fires once per overlay content rather than once per `effective_criteria` call, because it rides the existing routing cache; that the canonical replacement is the `{\"<id>\": [\"plan_review\"|\"code_review\"]}` mapping; and that removal is scheduled for v1.0.0. Documentation prose only — no `src` or test change, and no edit to any other section of the file.\n\n## Scope\nStep 5 adds `docs/release-notes.md` and nothing else. Out of scope: any change to `_activation_map` semantics or the other `CriteriaError` paths; the runtime behaviour of `assemble.py` and `schemas/__init__.py`; re-landing or amending steps 1-4, which are already on `origin/main`; and any edit to `CHANGELOG.md`, which this file's own header reserves for the user-facing feature/fix log.\n\n## Testing\nSteps 1-4 landed with `test_legacy_activate_list_warns_once(caplog)` and `test_canonical_activate_mapping_does_not_warn` in `tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py`, plus the `tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py` well-formedness tests covering the new row.\n\nStep 5 adds no test. `docs/release-notes.md` is hand-written prose with no generator and no drift gate — nothing regenerates it and no test asserts over its content — so a new test would pin wording rather than behaviour. Its correctness is checked by AC7 and AC8's greps and by `make verify`, which exercises the whole suite against the edited tree and so catches any repo-wide docs or link check the file does participate in.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `python -c \"from rebar._deprecations import REGISTRY; print(REGISTRY[\\\"cfg:criteria_routing.json 'activate' id-list\\\"].remove_in)\"` prints `v1.0.0`.\n- [x] The two new tests pass and `tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py::test_no_raw_deprecation_emissions` passes.\n- [x] `git grep -n -i \"single.pass\" -- src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py` prints nothing.\n- [x] `git grep -c \"logs a deprecation warning\" -- docs/plan-review-gate.md` prints `1`.\n- [x] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0 with no *unadmitted* new mechanism attributable to this ticket's paths. (Deviation on the record: this AC originally read \"reports `new=0`\". The script prints `active=650 new=27 increased=0 stale=0` and exits 0 because all 27 are admitted by in-tree `# mechanism-ok:` markers, and a pristine worktree at `origin/main` prints the identical line — so `new=0` was never true on this tree and is unmeetable as written. Replaced by the condition the gate actually enforces. Bug `6f24-3d47-b251-4905`.)\n- [x] `make verify` exits 0.\n- [ ] The entry is added and nothing else moved: `git grep -c '^## ' -- docs/release-notes.md` reports `65` against the pre-state of `64`; `sed -n '11p' docs/release-notes.md` is the new entry's `##` heading; and `git diff --numstat origin/main -- docs/release-notes.md` shows `0` deletions, confirming no existing section was altered.\n- [ ] The entry names the deprecated form and its replacement: over `docs/release-notes.md`, `git grep -c 'criteria_routing.json'` is at least `1` and `git grep -c 'activate'` is at least `1` (both pre-states `0`), and the new section's body contains the string `v1.0.0`.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the tree carrying the step-5 edit."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793443883539540001,"uuid":"403acc57-710c-4aac-bc58-792098481289"}